  "notes": "Two bounded variants of the behind-touch crown, both falsified as closers. capping per-level depth binds crown share without buying back empties (cap8: share 0.047, empty ~0.01): the emptied-touch channel depends on touch depth, which crown bounds don't set. Sizing crown orders heavier floods share past the tape's 0.21 uncapped (0.38) and suppresses the empty channel under every variant \u2014 visible depth and sweepability are the same variable in this grammar (order count = volume). The tape decouples them via hidden liquidity: hidden_depth.v1 measured 21.4% of fills printing inside the visible book. The residual is an iceberg crown \u2014 shadow depth behind the thin visible touch that only surfaces when the touch empties.",
